+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Memory auto-extraction (Story 8.8 kill-switch + Story 8.7 cost controls)
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# After every finalized assistant turn, a background Celery task asks the
+# workspace chat model to extract durable facts from the turn. That is one extra
+# LLM call per turn, so it is the single largest per-turn cost multiplier in the
+# product.
+#
+# Kill-switch (Story 8.8). Global default is ON. A workspace owner can also turn
+# it off individually via ``workspaces.memory_auto_extract_enabled``. Setting
+# this to false stops extraction everywhere without a redeploy, and is the
+# recommended posture until the recall eval-gate (G3) and the cost-control gate
+# (G4) are both closed — see _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/
